    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnănĭmis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		2. in-anima, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>without breath</i> or <i>without
			life</i>, <i>breathless</i>, <i>lifeless</i>, <i>inanimate</i> (Appuleian): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>that does not blow</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 103, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humi projectus, inanimis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			 p. 108, 25; cf. <i><span class="en">ib. 2, p. 125,
			41</span></i>. </div>
